WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
Imagine lending the federal
government 1,000 dollars by buying

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.480
one of its bonds.

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.130
It pays you a fixed 50 dollars a year,

4
00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.250
then repays the 1,000 when it matures.

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.340
You could hold cash instead.

6
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.930
Cash is easy to spend,

7
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.180
but it earns little or nothing.

8
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.550
So the bond seems like a good deal.

9
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.180
Yet bond owners sometimes
sell for less than they paid.

10
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.930
So why would anyone sell
a safe government bond

11
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.160
for less than they paid for it?

12
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.610
In this mission, you'll
weigh up liquidity,

13
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.810
return and risk for cash,

14
00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.030
bonds and stocks.

15
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.800
Then you'll use a graph lab to test what

16
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.870
moves a bond's price.

17
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: find out what
sets the price of a bond.
